WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.340 --> 00:00:04.420
Too many mussels can make for a sticky situation.

00:00:04.420 --> 00:00:06.180
Mussels are marine biofoulers,

00:00:06.180 --> 00:00:07.660
like barnacles and seaweed.

00:00:07.660 --> 00:00:09.240
They’ll take any opportunity to

00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:11.140
attach themselves to an object.

00:00:11.140 --> 00:00:12.500
They can clog pipes,

00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:14.500
destroy scientific equipment,

00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:16.480
and damage dams and boats.

00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:17.820
Researchers have spent decades

00:00:17.820 --> 00:00:19.340
trying to prevent mussels

00:00:19.340 --> 00:00:22.000
from attaching to everything they encounter.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:24.060
Now they've developed a polymer lubricant

00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:25.980
that prevents the mussels from attaching to

00:00:25.980 --> 00:00:27.800
underwater surfaces.

00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:30.980
The key to the mussel’s stickiness is byssal thread,

00:00:30.980 --> 00:00:32.760
a sticky fiber the animal secretes

00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:35.480
as soon as it detects a solid structure.

00:00:35.480 --> 00:00:37.480
The new lubricant repels organic matter

00:00:37.480 --> 00:00:39.680
so the scientists hypothesized that it would

00:00:39.680 --> 00:00:41.760
prevent the mussel from noticing the surface

00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:44.820
beneath them and initiating attachment.

00:00:44.820 --> 00:00:46.820
In testing, an asian green mussel

00:00:46.820 --> 00:00:49.440
poked its sticky appendage out at the surface…

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:52.659
but it couldn’t grab hold, the coating worked!

00:00:52.659 --> 00:00:54.370
The coating also worked In the field.

00:00:54.370 --> 00:00:56.900
After 8 weeks of submersion, plates coated

00:00:56.900 --> 00:00:58.320
with the polymer only averaged

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:00.560
4 mussels per square centimeter.

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:03.380
The control averaged 118.

00:01:03.380 --> 00:01:04.960
There is still testing to be done before

00:01:04.960 --> 00:01:07.460
this anti-mussel material will reach the market.

00:01:07.460 --> 00:01:09.660
But for scientists and sailors alike,

00:01:09.660 --> 00:01:11.480
it could be a life-saver.

